# Enterprise Document Intake — All Channels (CO-DOC-ARCH-001)

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Frozen · Permanent platform architecture  
Extends: Opportunity Document Center governance · CO-DOC-002 · Partner Gateway document projections

## Constitutional principles

1. **Catalyst One is the only Document SSOT.** One enterprise document architecture for all channels.
2. **Multiple intake channels · one store.** Walk-in, Direct/COMPASS, Wealth Partner (and future channels) feed the same Enterprise Document Registry / `EnterpriseTransactionDocument`.
3. **Source ≠ ownership.** `uploadSource` records where the file came from. Documents remain enterprise-owned.
4. **Upload ≠ verified ≠ requirement satisfied.** Lifecycle stays on Catalyst One Document Requests / registry verification — never channel-specific status engines.
5. **Requirements live in Catalyst One only.** LOD / EDIE / programme resolution must not be duplicated in COMPASS or Wealth Partner App.
6. **External UIs are presentation/intake only.** Partner App and COMPASS project checklist + pending items; they do not own documents.

## Canonical business channels → storage

Reuse existing `DocumentRegistryUploadSource` (do **not** invent parallel document models).

| Business channel | Storage `uploadSource` |
|---|---|
| `WALK_IN` | `manual_upload` |
| `DIRECT` | `customer_portal` |
| `WEALTH_PARTNER` | `wealth_partner` |

Also retained for other ingestion paths: `lender_portal`, `email`, `whatsapp`, `api`, `folder_package`, `conversation_activity`.

SSOT mapping: `src/constants/document-intake/`

## Forbidden

- `WealthPartnerDocument` / `CompassDocument` / `WalkInDocument` as separate SSOTs
- Separate document DBs, checklists, status engines, or intelligence engines in COMPASS / WP
- Hard-forcing external users to invent Deal IDs, lender programmes, or incorrect type/participant when unknown — prefer intake → Catalyst One classification/review
- Bypassing Partner Gateway / customer-token / internal permission authorization

